  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Assistance for Transitioning Housing Solutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to prevent homelessness among beneficiaries of International Protection (IP) and Temporary Protection (TP) in Belgium, France, and Greece. It supports their transition to sustainable housing and independent living through three pillars: 
 
Housing Platform Development &#x2013; A digital platform will connect beneficiaries with verified housing options, addressing challenges and reducing housing exclusion. 
 
Capacity Building for Intermediary Organizations &#x2013; National and regional networks will strengthen intermediary organizations&#x2019; capacity to improve housing access through knowledge sharing and best practices. 
 
Sensitization and Awareness &#x2013; Awareness campaigns will promote equal access to housing and foster solidarity among landlords, host communities, and other stakeholders. 
 
By addressing barriers to housing, building organizational capacity, and promoting inclusivity, the project ensures sustainable housing solutions for beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
